## Procedure

<!-- awf:include outline-approval -->

TDD may run without an effort. If continuity materially helps, invoke `{{ if index .skills "effort-workflow" }}{{ .prefix }}-effort-workflow{{ else }}the effort lifecycle owner{{ end }}` before mutation; if an effort already exists, validate its fixed identity and exact `.awf/efforts/<slug>/memory.md`, preserve one writer, and give that context read-only to helpers. Otherwise omit effort and memory fields. {{if eq .profile "core"}}Project documentation, source, tests, and repository history{{else}}Repository and current-state authority{{end}} remain primary, and standalone memory is forbidden.

1. {{if ne .profile "core"}}Use CodeGraph when discovery or a structural question exists, then run `./awf resolve topic <the implementation and verification paths>` and read applicable topics before you {{end}}select the strongest practical durable oracle under the rule above for a bug fix. For the normal fix path, write the failing test capturing the wrong behaviour. For a fix-only alternative, record the concrete reason automated red-first is impractical and prepare the selected reproducible evidence. For feature work, write the failing automated test capturing the missing behaviour; the alternative-oracle path does not widen to features. Ground tests, checks, seams, and harness work only in changed behavior, a demonstrated regression, an existing documented contract, or a clearly applicable project invariant; reject speculative test or policy machinery.
2. Exercise the selected oracle before implementation. For an automated bug regression or feature test, run it and confirm it fails for the right reason{{ with .vars.testCmd }}: `{{ . }}`{{ end }}. For a fix-only alternative, reproduce the unfixed behaviour safely and retain the inputs, expected result, actual evidence, and concrete reason.
3. Before implementing, per `{{ .layout.maintainableCodeDesign }}`, assess whether a bounded enabling refactor prevents duplication, coupling, representation leakage, or a workaround.
<!-- awf:include clean-integration -->
<!-- awf:include implementation-autonomy -->
Route materially larger work through {{ if .skills.brainstorming }}`{{ .prefix }}-brainstorming`{{ else }}the active workflow's design discussion{{ end }} to
<!-- awf:include escalation-menu -->
Choose the smallest behavior-proving, model-supporting seam; reject tests that force representation leakage or needless indirection.
4. Implement the minimal root-cause change that satisfies the selected oracle.
5. Run the selected behavior-proving oracle and the narrowest relevant owner check.

